  "changes": [
    {
      "location": "FileClose, FClose, and TstMod entries",
      "change": "Removed later vectors and the process-ownership close patch. Restored the original FileClose, GetEOF, and SetEOF names.",
      "evidence": "FileClose calls FSQueue directly at 0x40514e. FClose saves its return address at 0x405168, and TstMod calls RfNCall at 0x40539c. The ROM retains the October 1985 RfNCall and AdjEOF vectors. The provisional exported DoClosePop name at 0x40514e came from later patched source; FileClose is the entry represented by the ROM."
    },
    {
      "location": "FClose B-tree and truncate paths",
      "change": "Restored closing all associated B-tree control blocks and the earlier clump-rounding path. Removed the later guard for other open paths to the same fork.",
      "evidence": "At 0x405176, a nonzero FCBBTCBPtr leads to BTClose or BTFlush without the later FSUsrCNID restriction. ResetAEOF begins at 0x4051b2 with the FlushOnly test, then calls TstMod. The ROM retains the commented RoundAlloc sequence at 0x4051ca through 0x4051e4 and calls TruncateFile without a D2 option. It has no later second dirty-bit clear."
    },
    {
      "location": "Fixed file control block size",
      "change": "Restored FCBEntLen expressions in the close cleanup and reference-number check.",
      "evidence": "The clearing loop loads 46 at 0x4052da to clear 47 words. CkFileRfn divides by immediate 94 at 0x405380. Both values match the original fixed-size FCB definition, before the February 1987 FSFCBLen conversion."
    },
    {
      "location": "FndFCB",
      "change": "Removed the January 1986 VCB-pointer assignment for lookup by reference number.",
      "evidence": "After CkFileRfn at 0x40545e, the ROM tests D0 and returns. The surviving source adds MOVE.L FCBVPtr(A1,D1),A2 at that point. The reconstruction retains the ROM behavior, including this missing setup for the non-indexed path."
    },
    {
      "location": "FileAlloc and SetEOF interfaces",
      "change": "Restored allocation through Alloc and AllocContig and truncation through FlushOnly.",
      "evidence": "toAlloc at 0x405476 tests the volume and HFS bit, then branches to Alloc at 0x4055be or AllocContig at 0x4055ce. Its MFS path clears D0 before AllocSt. SetEOF sets FlushOnly at 0x405508 and calls TruncateFile without the later kTFTrunExt option in D2."
    },
    {
      "location": "Definitions, inactive code, and encoding",
      "change": "Copied original equates, supplied external addresses, and made PC-relative JSR operands explicit. Retained the original IF 0 blocks as comments and marked this change. Preserved the original header, applicable history, and comments.",
      "evidence": "The disabled range-lock bodies remain available for review and emit no bytes. The three FClose branches expanded in 1992 use their original short encodings here. SetEOF and FileAlloc calls to AdjEOF and the branch to MFSShrtnF use word displacements. All 1,082 bytes and 37 recorded labels match."
    }
  ],
